# Phase 4 evaluation fixture for tests/bench_memory_digest.py
#
# One JSON object per line. Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#   {"half", "srcip", "action", "verdict", "notes", "recorded_by"}
#
# action is "verdict" (the default) or "invalidate", which withdraws the reason
# whose text matches notes. half is "tune" or "gate": the digest parameter is chosen
# on the tune half and the gate half is measured once, after the parameter is frozen.
#
# Property coverage, one row set per property. Both halves carry every property so a
# gate half cannot pass because the hard cases happen to live in the tune half:
#   repeated subjects          : .200, .201, .205, .206, .207, .208, .211 appear more than
#                                once, with five runs on .200 and .206
#   multiple decisions         : .200, .205, .206, .207, .211 hold two or more verdicts
#   repeated reasons           : .201 and .211 repeat a note (folded by Phase 3)
#   contradictory verdicts     : .200, .206, .207 hold analyst false_positive and analyst true_positive
#   analyst-authoritative      : every row with recorded_by analyst
#   workflow decisions         : .203, .205, .209 and one run each of .200 and .206
#   tainted reasons            : every reason
#   invalidated memory         : .202 and .208 each withdraw one reason
#   unrelated subjects         : .204 and .210 hold a single verdict
#   sparse history             : .203 and .209 hold one decision
#   enough history to benefit  : .200 and .206 hold eight units each
#   prompt injection in a reason: .201 (tune) and .207 (gate)
#
# STATUS: FIXTURE, synthetic. Subjects are in 203.0.113.0/24 (RFC 5737) and every
# note was written for this file. No production data, no real indicator.
